# This image copies nothing. The repo, mcp/server.py included, arrives as a bind
# mount at /asset-engine, so the build context only has to be big enough to hold
# the Dockerfile itself, which Docker reads separately.
#
# Excluding everything keeps it that way: the build context is tarred and handed
# to the daemon before the first instruction is read, cached build or not, and a
# context that quietly grows is a build that quietly slows. If a COPY is ever
# added here, un-ignore exactly the file it copies and nothing else.
*
